There shall be eight standing committees comprised of three members each as follows:
(1) Utilities planning and operation, streets and sanitation;
(2) Licensing and inspections, alcohol beverage control;
(3) Community relations, library;
(4) Budget, Charter and legislative;
(5) Public property, planning and zoning;
(6) Cemetery;
(7) Public safety emergency operations; and
(8) Personnel.
On or before January 15, 2004 and on or before January 15 of each biennial year thereafter, the members of each committee shall be chosen by three members of the council consisting of the mayor pro tem, and two other members of the council elected by the council. Each council committee, except for public safety emergency operations, shall consist of three council members. The public safety emergency operations committee shall consist of the mayor and two council members. Each committee shall elect its chairperson.
Any member of the Byron city council, including the mayor of Byron, shall be entitled to attend and observe any and all committee meetings, and/or any parts thereof, including, but not limited to, the executive session portion of said meetings, regardless of whether said council member or mayor is a member of said committee. The foregoing allowance provides for attendance and observation only, except as provided and/or allowed by the chair of the committee, the non-committee member shall not participate in said committee meeting, nor have any obligations, voting powers, or responsibilities regarding the committee meeting. Said non-committee member may or may not be recognized by the chair in the chair's sole discretion, to address the committee or make any comment(s) in said committee meeting and/or part thereof.
(Code 1935, § 57; Code 1987, § 2-29; Ord. No. 2003-21, § 2-29, 12-31-2003; Ord. No. 2021-1, 3-8-2021; Ord. No. 2021-3, 3-8-2021)

